                  27.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3">Matthew xxiv, 15; Mark, xiii, 14.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4">
          <foreign xml:lang="grc">θρόνος</foreign>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5">This passage to '<placeName>Jerusalem</placeName>' (1. 16) is
                  published in Greek with the heading <foreign xml:lang="grc">Σεβήρου</foreign> in Mai,
                  <foreign xml:lang="ln">Scriptorum Veterum Nova Collectio</foreign>, I, 11, 213. Gr. <foreign xml:lang="grc">φάμεν</foreign>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6">Jo. Chrys., Adv. Jud. v. 10, 11 (ed. Par. 2a, I, 788).</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7">Or Man.,
                  10.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8">Or
                  'literal'. Gr. <foreign xml:lang="grc">κατὰ τὴν τῆς ἱστ. ἀπόδοσιν</foreign>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9">2 Thessalonians 11, 4.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10">Jo. Chrys., op. cit., v, 10 (ed. Par. 2a, I, 788). The
                  text differs widely.</note>
      </noteGrp>
